  "status": "Application Under Consideration",
  "description": "Benthal Primary School is a 2 Form Entry Primary School, located between Stoke Newington and Lower Clapton in the London Borough of Hackney.\nThe school is formed around 2No main buildings; the Infant School, built around 1965, and the Junior School, which was completed around 1947 following the end of WWII. Occupants of both the Junior School and the Infant School have reported issues around overheating within classrooms and other spaces with large areas of glazing alongside the generally poor condition of the ageing windows and rooflights. In response to this, the London Borough of Hackney are proposing the rectification of this issue by way of:\n\nJunior School \n- Removal of existing single-pane steel Crittall style windows.\n- Localised removal of textured asbestos ceiling portions.\n- Installation of a new set of replacement double-glazed aluminium window units with transoms/mullions to match existing.\n- Making good of internal/external areas affected by window replacement. \n- Localised repairs to key areas of structure.\n\nInfant School \n- Replacement of existing rooflight hinges/hardware and with new components. \n- Application of G-Value solar control film to rooflight glazing. \n\n",
